You are the first
celebrity I’ve met.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.689
I am? 

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.857
Oh my goodness! 

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.650
Who's your
favorite character?

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.111
My favorite character is
Ash and you.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:29.237
Thank you. 

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:30.280
Hey!

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:32.699
Wow. “That’s your enemy”
is that what you said?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.742
No they’re with the Academy.

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:34.743
Oh, with the Academy.
Hello!

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:35.660
You’re shivering.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.369
Yeah.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.537
They’ve got to give you
 a space heater 

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.830
or something.
Campbell's soup? 

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.957
You are my favorite
 character in the movie.

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:41.916
Oh yay! 

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:43.251
Yes, that’s awesome. 

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:44.669
(music)

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:47.839
Oh, my goodness. 

00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:48.965
What's your name? 

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:50.425
My name's Kaylin Golchini 

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.052
and I think you're a star. 

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.261
Oh, thank you.

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:56.181
I can’t wait to meet
the two legends.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.852
How is it
singing with Bono?

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.773
When I was your age,
 I was like the biggest

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:06.483
fan of his band, U2, 

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:09.527
and so it was like
 my dream come true.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.570
So if it could
happen to me, 

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.197
it could happen to you!

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:13.656
Who would you
want to sing with?

00:01:13.656 --> 00:01:15.450
I would want to
 sing with you. 

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.868
No way!

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:19.537
I got you an early
 Christmas gift.

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:20.705
Can I open it now?

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:21.873
Yeah!

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:23.875
I think you earned it. 

00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:25.418
Did you get me an Oscar? 

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:28.296
Proud moment.

00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:30.423
Shall I just
walk up and down? 

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.008
I think he likes it. 

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:35.470
I just want to say you're
 amazing and hilarious

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.639
at changing your voice. 

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:39.349
(funny voice)
Thank you so much. 

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:40.558
Beep beep boop boop.

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:41.643
Was that good?

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:43.061
That's amazing!

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:44.187
He did the “beep beep”

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:50.151
Do adults love animated
 movies just as kids do?

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:51.152
I think so. 

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:53.363
Animation has been
around for 100 years, 

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:54.948
so adults grew
up on animation. 

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.825
And adults are
always looking for 

00:01:56.825 --> 00:01:58.910
something to do
with their kids 

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.203
and also
 distract their kids 

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.746
because they're
very tired. 

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:04.749
Their kids
 are killing them.

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:08.128
Slowly. It's a slow
death, but they're 

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.963
the kids are designed
 to replace the adults 

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.256
and they're just
tearing them down. 

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:12.966
So, you know, 

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.884
when you have kids, you're
 just so exhausted. 

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.344
Anything that gets
your kid’s attention

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:17.345
you're like, “thank God.”

00:02:18.555 --> 00:02:19.597
Yeah something
to think about.

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:20.932
It’s a lot.
It’s heavy.

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:21.933
Nice meeting you. 

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:23.852
Yeah thanks, I think that's
 where we should end it.

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.061
(laughter)

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.479
That's a wrap! 

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.856
Back to you Academy.

